PRODUCT: Agentic Office, an agentic workspace where Word, Excel and PowerPoint files live together. An assistant drafts edits across files as tracked changes/diffs; a person accepts or rejects each one. Audience: consultants, finance teams, lawyers. Approved truths: one request updated model (Revenue!E6 8.9→8.5), memo (€71–73m→€74.6m) and deck (Slide 4 title, Slide 2 TextBox 23 etc.); 10 changes across 3 files, all reviewable; real recording sped up. Do NOT claim time savings or unattended approval.
FILM: "Done." V33, 95 s, 16:9, master -14.1 LUFS / -1.8 dBTP, VO-led ducking. Fictional illustration UIs (unbranded chatbot, Word/Excel/PowerPoint/PDF look-alikes, email client) in the first half; REAL product screenshots/recording in the second half (labelled). Real stock footage (Mixkit/Pexels): one protagonist (Black woman, striped shirt, blue night office) in 2 clips, plus hands/phone/mouse/sunrise inserts. Kokoro TTS draft narrator (af_heart) + one British male voice reading the partner's email.
SHOTS (s): 0–4.5 FIRST FRAME: cards "FY26_Model.xlsx €74.6m" ≠ "Board_Presentation.pptx Slide 4 €71–73m" over the email to the partner with 3 attachments (Board_Memo_Q3.docx, FY26_Model.xlsx, Board_Presentation.pptx), cursor on Send, red clock 8:57 AM · BOARD AT 9:00 · 4.5–5 rewind glitch · 5–8 protagonist at desk (real), super "45 MINUTES EARLIER"; 8.0–8.7 eased dark-to-light transition into the chat · 8–11 chatbot: "Hi, how can I help?", prompt typed "DACH Q4 is now 8.5. Update the board memo." (same change the real product half performs), reply streams · 11–12.4 giant "✓ Done." (#1) · 12.4–15.6 Word-like window opens Board_Memo_Q3.docx, glitch on "wrecked", flags Template gone / Numbering wrong / Table shifted · 15.6–16.5 real hands typing insert · 16.5–23 fixing by hand; partner email notification enlarges and is read aloud · 23–24 protagonist head in hands (real) · 24–27.5 asks chatbot "Now update the board deck to match the memo" (night hands insert); "Generating presentation…" slide thumbnails fill · 27.5–28.3 "✓ Done. AGAIN." (#2) · 28.4–31.0 partner: "The deck still says €71–73m. The model says €74.6m. Fix slide 2." held 2.6 s; VO "But the deck still has the old number.", ring on slide 2 · 30–35 re-prompt; "Regenerating all 12 slides… about 5 min left" progress crawl; red clock time-lapse 8:41→8:46; super "Five minutes. For one number."; insert: she scratches her head (real) · 34.5–35.2 "✓ Done. AND AGAIN." (#3, ghosted, shaking) · 35–37.4 deck regenerated: slide 2 ✓ but slide 4 reverted to €71–73m, ringed red; her frustrated reaction (real) · 37.4–41.6 whip pans across Word/Excel/PowerPoint/PDF/chat with giant words Copy. Paste. Check. Repeat.; windows pile up, notifications stack, clock 8:52→8:59 · 41.6–46 back at the email; notification "Are these the final files? The client is waiting." held 2.7 s; cursor drifts onto Send and STOPS; total silence; 44.55 insert: she drops her head onto the desk (real) · 46–55 ONE continuous reveal: logo + "See exactly what changed. Decide what stays.", then real Word/Excel/PowerPoint screenshots fan in from 50.2 (real UI screenshots shown inside a blurred real office background, not on black), real Word/Excel/PowerPoint screenshots fan in and merge · 55–60 "It finds." real prompt typed in the real app, framed tight on the prompt text (no model picker in frame) ("Take DACH Q4 down to 8.5… make the memo and the deck match… Show me the diffs"), agent working, sped up · 60–64.4 "It fixes." real Excel bar "Revenue!E6 8.9 → 8.5 Reject/Accept", real memo tracked change €71–73m→€74.6m · 64.4–72.6 "You decide." REAL RECORDING of the Changes panel: 0 of 10 → Accept all clicked → "All changes reviewed · 10 of 10" (no simulated cursor); real "All changes reviewed · 10 of 10" list scrolls; red ring on "Slide 4 title €71–73m → €74.6m"; callout "The slide that slipped. Slide 4. Caught." · 72.6–76.6 "Bring in your team." real app Room (demo session, simulated teammate, labelled): Alex Morgan (you), Priya Raman, Priya's Assistant posting its plan · 76.6–79.4 "Only a person says yes." real: "Priya's Assistant proposes 1 edit · Replace €71–73m with €74.6m · Accept / Reject", buttons ringed · 79.4–82.6 "Your workspace. Your files, stored on your device." real file tree + real status bar "Local · Default Approvals · Can make mistakes" + on-screen "Cloud AI may process document content." · 82.6–86 back at the same email; real hand clicks mouse; "✓ Sent · Memo · model · deck · every change reviewed" (no clock) · 86–89 real sunrise through office window (warm grade, first warm shot) · 89–95 "AI said it was done." struck through → "This time, you checked." → logo, "See exactly what changed. Decide what stays.", "Request early access".
AUDIO TIMELINE: cold open: buzz, bass pulse, fast heartbeat · rewind sfx · 5–17 light lounge bed (Mixkit "Hazy After Hours", licensed) + office room tone, typing, send pop · DONE CHIME (same sound) at 11.05 (soft), 27.5 (louder), 34.45 (loudest, echoed ×4) · glitch+static on "wrecked" · phone buzz on email, jazz dies, suspense bed from 17.3 · bass pulse from 28.3, slow heartbeat 30.8–35, clock ticking time-lapse, swell to Done #3 · whooshes per whip, impact on "Repeat.", riser into overload · 41.6 heartbeat only; 43.6 everything cuts to room tone (silence) under "The worst part…" · 46.2 a new soft identity tone · 49.6 calm confident electronic bed (Mixkit "Digital Clouds") · one UI tick per visible edit, soft pop on Accept · 72.6 music dips, heartbeat, mouse click at 74.55, identity tone on "Sent" · music returns under dawn with morning city ambience and birds, then end card. All music/SFX Mixkit free licence, footage Mixkit/Pexels licence, per-file provenance logged.

VO LINES (exact): 0.4s Nine A.M. Board meeting. And the deck doesn't match the model. | 6.0s You ask a chatbot to update the board memo. | 11.0s It says it's done. | 12.5s Then you open the file... and the formatting's wrecked. | 15.55s So you fix it by hand. Then, an email. | 18.15s Please update the model and the board deck to match, before the meeting. | 24.0s So you ask it for the deck... and it builds one, in the chat. | 28.35s But the deck still has the old number. | 30.2s Prompt again. Wait again. Five minutes... for one number. | 34.6s Done. Except now... slide four changed. | 37.6s Five tabs. Copy. Paste. Check. Repeat. | 42.3s The worst part? You don't even know what's wrong anymore. | 46.3s See exactly what changed. Decide what stays. | 49.9s Meet Agentic Office. Your Word, Excel and PowerPoint, in one workspace. | 55.1s Tell it what changed. Once. | 57.0s It finds where that number lives: the model, the memo, the deck. | 60.45s And drafts each fix in place, for you to review. | 64.6s Every change is marked, in every file. You accept it, or reject it. | 69.6s Even slide four. | 72.8s Bring in your team. People, and their assistants, on the same files. | 76.8s Every proposal still waits for a person. | 79.5s Your workspace. Your files, stored on your device. | 85.2s Done. And this time, you've seen every change. | 92.6s Agentic Office.
